lib — PDP-11 target runtime
===========================

The object files the linker pulls in for a PDP-11 program: the C runtime
startup and the C library.  They install to `${libdir}/v7unix/`.

  crt0.s  fcrt0.s  mcrt0.s  fmcrt0.s   V7 /usr/src/libc/csu sources, kept
                                       unmodified; `make` assembles them with
                                       our own `as` into the .o files.  The
                                       assembled .o are byte-identical to the
                                       V7 disk image's (verified).
  build-libc.sh                       builds `libc.a` from V7's own
                                       /usr/src/libc (orig/usr/src/libc/): it
                                       compiles each source (compall order)
                                       with the ported cc/as, then archives the
                                       members (mklib order) into a V7-format
                                       archive with tools/mkvar.py.

`libc.a` carries csv/cret/cerror, the arithmetic helpers, printf, write, exit,
and the rest of V7's C library, compiled by our own toolchain.  Its member
bytes are byte-identical to the V7 disk image's `/lib/libc.a` (152 of 153
members; `doscan.o` differs by a c2 peephole-optimizer gap, see PORTING.md).
The archive timestamp differs, being a fresh build.
